      "bot": "I'd be happy to help you analyze the medical image. However, I don't see any image attached to your message. Could you please provide more context or describe the image you'd like me to analyze? This will help me provide more accurate and relevant general health insights.\n\nIf you're unable to share the image, I can still offer general guidance on what might be visible in a medical image, such as:\n\n1. General observations about what might be visible:\n   - Skin lesions or rashes\n   - Abnormal growths or tumors\n   - Swelling or inflammation\n   - Abnormalities in the eyes, ears, or other body parts\n   - Changes in skin texture or color\n\n2. Possible non-diagnostic information:\n   - Age-related changes\n   - Lifestyle-related changes (e.g., sun damage, smoking)\n   - Nutritional deficiencies\n   - Environmental factors (e.g., exposure to chemicals)\n\n3. When professional consultation is needed:\n   - Any unusual or unexplained changes\n   - Symptoms that are causing discomfort or pain\n   - Changes that are rapidly progressing or worsening\n   - Concerns about potential health risks or complications\n\n4. Important: This is NOT a diagnosis, only general information\n   - Any medical image should be evaluated by a qualified healthcare professional for accurate diagnosis and treatment.\n\nPlease provide more context or describe the image you'd like me to analyze, and I'll do my best to provide general health insights.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f IMPORTANT: This analysis is NOT a diagnosis. Please consult a qualified healthcare professional for proper medical examination and diagnosis."
