      "timestamp": "2026-02-05T18:42:19.518287",
      "user": "what is acne?",
      "bot": "Acne is a common skin condition characterized by the occurrence of pimples, blackheads, and other lesions on the skin, particularly on the face, chest, and back. It is caused by a combination of factors, including:\n\n- Overproduction of oil (sebum) by the skin's sebaceous glands\n- Clogged pores due to dead skin cells and other debris\n- Bacteria (Propionibacterium acnes) that thrive in the pores and cause inflammation\n- Hormonal fluctuations, which can lead to increased oil production and pore clogging\n\nAcne can be classified into different types, including:\n\n- Non-inflammatory acne (blackheads and whiteheads)\n- Inflammatory acne (papules, pustules, and nodules)\n- Cystic acne (large, painful cysts)\n\nIf you're experiencing acne symptoms, I recommend using our Symptom Checker service to assess your condition and get personalized advice."
    },
